# Cloudflare Pages path redirects. Format: <source> <target> <status>. The first match wins, and a
# redirect fires even when a file exists at the source, so a path that is routed again must leave
# this file in the same change (tests/redirects.test.mjs enforces it). Static rules come before the
# splat rules. Host-level redirects (www, .dev) are a Cloudflare rule, not this file (REQ-017,
# docs/ops/canonical-host.md). Every target is a fixed path on this site: no placeholder, no
# external host, no query string (no open redirect; tests/redirects.test.mjs enforces it).
#
# Deliberately NOT redirected (they return the real 404): /auth and /dashboard (unrouted app pages
# with no public equivalent, STS-016; robots.txt does not list them, since a Disallow line would
# only advertise them) and the never-built footer links of the original template (/newsroom,
# /documentation, /support).

